{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && sed -n '1,80p' check-harness-tcp.go && echo \\\"=== plan ===\\\" && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('check-plan-tcp.json'));print(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:2500])\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\n \"description\": \"Second scenario of the same requirement, fixed on the production transport: the first check exercised the interleaving with a substitute StreamLayer, and this one uses the real NetworkTransport over the TCP stream layer instead, leaving everything else identical. Discriminator: a node is bootstrapped with both voters, a StableStore wrapper is armed, a heartbeat-shaped AppendEntries is sent so the transport's own classification invokes the registered callback on its connection goroutine, that callback's CurrentTerm write is held, a higher-term AppendEntries is then sent through the main loop on a second connection, and the held write is released. Observation: the harness reports the term the node acknowledged for the higher-term request, the term context in effect afterwards, the sequence of CurrentTerm writes the injected store saw, the transport kind and the local address; the assertion compares the observed context term with the admitted term. Control: the same node and caller policy as the substitute-layer scenario, with the transport kind reported so the two executions cannot be confused; the harness skips when the TCP transport cannot bind rather than reporting a result.\",\n \"claim_id\": \"c-adopted-term-never-regresses\",\n \"binding_ids\": [\n  \"bind-raft-process-heartbeat\"\n ],\n \"harness\": {\n  \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n  \"description\": \"TestAssuranceHeartbeatTermContextOverTCP: the term-context interleaving over the production TCP transport\",\n  \"source\": \"\",\n  \"files\": {},\n  \"semantic_changes\": [\n   \"No target file is modified; the harness adds one external test file to the captured package.\",\n   \"Both endpoints are NewTCPTransport instances bound to 127.0.0.1, so the transport, its heartbeat classification, the callback invocation on its connection goroutine and the wire encoding are the target's own code; the substitute fabric of the first scenario is absent.\",\n   \"StableStore is an InmemStore wrapper that holds exactly one CurrentTerm write inside SetUint64, the same latency injection the first scenario used.\",\n   \"The harness skips when the TCP transport cannot bind, so an environment without a usable loopback records an unavailable execution rather than a result.\"\n  ],\n  \"prerequisites\": [\n   {\n    \"alias\": \"admit\",\n    \"event\": \"term_advanced\",\n    \"conditions\": []\n   }\n  ],\n  \"legality\": {\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-raft-process-heartbeat\",\n    \"s-net-fastpath\",\n    \"s-net-handle-conn\",\n    \"s-net-set-heartbeat\",\n    \"s-raft-append-term\",\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
