{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_11-29-07-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('submissions/570a9a897e8e40f79783c59af539eba1/raw.json'))\nprint('top keys:', list(d.keys()))\nc=d.get('candidate',{})\nprint('candidate keys:', list(c.keys()))\nq=c.get('question',{})\nprint('question keys:', list(q.keys()))\nprint()\nprint('QUESTION TEXT:', q.get('question'))\nprint()\nprint('IMPORTANCE:', (q.get('importance') or '')[:1200])\nprint()\nprint('TRIGGER:', (q.get('trigger_rationale') or '')[:900])\nprint()\nprint('principal fact_ids:', q.get('fact_ids'), '| behavior_ids:', q.get('behavior_ids'), '| supporting:', q.get('supporting_behavior_ids'))\nprint('lifecycle:', q.get('lifecycle'))\nprint()\nprint('OBLIGATION:', json.dumps(c.get('obligation'), indent=1)[:1500])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"top keys: ['action', 'rationale', 'candidate', 'plan_path', 'harness_path']\ncandidate keys: ['action', 'rationale', 'map_path', 'map_changes', 'question', 'obligation', 'bindings']\nquestion keys: ['question', 'importance', 'trigger_rationale', 'disposition', 'preferred_check', 'participants', 'objects', 'contexts', 'event_paths', 'activity_classes', 'behavior_ids', 'fact_ids', 'supporting_behavior_ids', 'obligation_relation_kind', 'counterevidence', 'unknowns', 'priority', 'source_ids']\n\nQUESTION TEXT: Does Raft.GetConfiguration report, through its future, the log index at which the configuration it returns was established - as the accessor's contract and the metric built on it require - or does it return a configuration with an index that does not identify it?\n\nIMPORTANCE: The configuration future is the only way a client can obtain the cluster's current participant set, and its index is the only way to relate that set to a log position: a caller cannot tell whether the configuration it received corresponds to the state it is looking at, cannot detect that a configuration change happened between two reads by comparing indexes, and cannot distinguish a real configuration from none at all. The same value is published as latest_configuration_index in Stats, so monitoring that watches that metric always sees zero and can never observe configuration changes. The consequence is a client-contract one rather than a safety one, but the value is wrong for every call.\n\nTRIGGER: The accessor builds its future from the copy of the latest configuration that the lock-free readers use and sets only the configuration field, leaving the index field at its zero value, while the accessor's own contract describes the index of the applied log entry and Stats publishes the same field as a metric. A single-voter bootstrap makes the comparison unambiguous, because the configuration entry is the only entry in the log and its index is therefore the log's last index.\n\nprincipal fact_ids: ['f-latest-configuration'] | behavior_ids: ['b-config-change', 'b-client-apply-verify'] | supporting: {'b-follower-append-entries': 'shows the same fact is established from the log on followers, so the reported index is part of the established fact rather than a leader-only artefact', 'b-commit-advance': 'shows the configuration is consumed as the qualifying voter set, which is why its identity and index matter to the support line'}\nlifecycle: None\n\nOBLIGATION: {\n \"id\": \"c-reported-configuration-index\",\n \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n \"description\": \"The configuration future returned by Raft.GetConfiguration must report, as its index, the log index at which the configuration it returns was established, so that a caller can relate the participant set it receives to a position in the replicated log and to the value the library publishes for the same future.\",\n \"source_ids\": [\n  \"s-api-get-configuration\",\n  \"s-api-stats-config-index\",\n  \"s-raft-append-config\",\n  \"s-api-newraft-config\"\n ],\n \"scope\": {\n  \"description\": \"A node in the captured module answering a client's GetConfiguration call, with the configuration established either by bootstrap or by a configuration entry.\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n   \"the caller reads the future's Index as the index of the configuration it received\",\n   \"the configuration copy read by the accessor is the latest one, as its own comment states\"\n  ],\n  \"excluded\": [\n   \"the correctness of the configuration value itself, which the check reads back\",\n   \"the voter-set and commitment semantics that consume the configuration\",\n   \"any requirement on callers or transports outside the module\"\n  ]\n },\n \"pending\": [\n  \"which consumers rely on the index\",\n  \"whether the repair carries the index with the copy or routes the accessor through the main loop\"\n ],\n \"grounding\": {\n  \"source_ids\": [\n   \"s-api-get-configuration\",\n   \"s-api-stats-config-index\",\n   \"s-raft-append-config\",\n   \"s-api\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
