s-api-get-configuration); the accessor's index is documented as the index of the applied log entry and is published as latest_configuration_index in Stats (s-api-stats-config-index); and the index a configuration is established at is the log index of its entry, which for a bootstrapped node is the entry appended during bootstrap (s-api-newraft-config, s-raft-append-config). The obligation therefore requires the reported index to be that log index for the configuration the future returns.\",\n    \"applicability\": \"Applies to any node answering GetConfiguration; the check exercises a bootstrapped single-voter node where the configuration entry is the only log entry, so the comparison has a single unambiguous value.\",\n    \"unresolved\": [\n     \"whether the index is intentionally omitted off the main loop, which no source states\",\n     \"whether any consumer depends on the value\"\n    ],\n    \"conflicts\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": [\n     \"the zero could be read as an unset placeholder, but the library publishes it as a metric and the accessor's contract names a real index\"\n    ]\n   }\n  },\n  \"bindings\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"bind-raft-get-configuration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"s-api-get-configuration\",\n    \"symbol\": \"GetConfiguration\",\n    \"start_line\": 897,\n    \"end_line\": 903,\n    \"description\": \"Raft.GetConfiguration builds a configurations value from the copy of the latest configuration and responds immediately, so the future it returns carries the live configuration with an index field that is never set on this path.\",\n    \"pending\": [\n     \"whether the index should travel with the atomic copy or be fetched from the main loop\"\n    ],\n    \"associations\": [\n     {\n      \"claim_id\": \"c-reported-configuration-index\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n       \"s-api-get-configuration\",\n       \"s-api-stats-config-index\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"This entry point is the located implementation of the reporting duty: it returns the configuration a caller asked for but omits the index that identifies where that configuration was established, and the same omitted field is what Stats publishes as a metric.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"plan_path\": \"check-plan-config.json\",\n \"harness_path\": \"check-harness-config.go\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
